  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">DRRS BiH Scoping 2025 &#x2013; Team Leader</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">A severe storm brought heavy rainfall over southern and central Bosnia and Herzegovina (BiH) on 3 and 4 October 2024, which triggered flash floods and landslides. The municipality of Jablanica, was particularly hard-hit. The city of Konjic, and the municipalities of Buturovic polje, Fojnica, Kiseljak and Kre&#x161;evo were also severely affected. Roads, bridges, and railway tracks were washed away orobstructed by debris.After the recent events in central Bosnia and Herzegovina (BiH), protection against the harmful effects of water again becomes particularly relevant due to the atastrophic consequences for human life, health, infrastructure, economy and all spheres of life in BiH. Governmental institutions and organizations want to increase the flexibility of existing and future strategies, programs, projects and investments to prevent the occurrence of such and similar disasters.Based on the provided information, Dutch Disaster Risk Reduction and Surge Support (DRRS) has been asked by the Embassy of the Netherlands in BiH to do a short scoping on the DRR-responsibilities in early warning, early action and flood risk management, and policy gaps in the local communities (LGUs).</narrative>
  </description>
